Umoria Version 5.5, patch level 0


                        Moria Supreme
Moria Supreme is a free hobby build of Pmoria 0.98. It keeps the
Wilson/Koeneke notices and Koeneke's no-sale dedication. It is not
relicensed, and it will not be sold.

Races added beside the Pmoria set: Gnome (the Umoria race Pmoria had
replaced with the Spectre) and Dryad. Classes added: Druid, Bard, and
Adventurer. Their numbers are original. See docs/VARIANTS.md.

The town has a hall, a bank, a notice board, a hidden guild door,
four patrons, bard instruments, and a grove book for druids.

Birth asks for a temperament. The bank has a locker. The board can
post a wanted notice. Unknown weapons and armor have a feeling, and
the hall can read armor. A pack item inscribed "junk" can be
destroyed with }, and a spectre can spend a wand charge with ]. A
character under a fifth of their hit points is asked before taking
stairs. The general store can stock a travel loaf.

This game is save version 1.0. A character history records level
gains, a new deepest floor, the first ego item, a winning creature,
a temple dedication, and a finished notice-board job. A reads the
log. Birth can turn on randomized ego items (the same Moria names,
with bonuses moved by at most one), ironman stairs, no selling, or
connected stairs. Each one starts off. Floor gold is doubled when
selling is off.

Goblins, wargs, a giant wood spider, and a stone troll live in the
dungeon. The troll stiffens in daylight or lamplight. A pale riddler
asks one riddle, once. The prize is a ring of invisibility, which
adds stealth. A weapon of Orc-warning glows when orc-kin are in
sight. Deep down, a dragon sometimes sits on extra gold. Halflings
are a little better at slipping locks and moving quietly.

An older save or score file is refused. Moria Supreme 1.0 will not
load Pmoria, Umoria, or an earlier Moria Supreme character.

This build runs on Linux, on macOS, and in a web browser. The DOS,
Atari ST, Amiga, Mac Classic, VMS, and IBM PC sources are not in the
tree. The credits above for those ports stay.
